From 5a38552fbcdb6e7b7d31500732a97cb5573e6e1d Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: t <tristan75015@gmail.com>
Date: Sat, 10 Oct 2026 02:35:34 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] Acceleration algorithms of MTest for the fixed point solver

- Anderson's method: options `Period` (accelerations every `Period`
  iterations, the histories being updated at each iteration) and
  `Residuals` (`Unknowns`: fixed point residuals; `Forces`: residuals of
  the problem); `UAnderson` and `FAnderson` declared with the defaults of
  MTest (period 2);
- ports of the algorithms of MTest based on secant and delta squared
  methods: `Secant`, `CrossedSecant`, `AlternateSecant`, `IronsTuck`,
  `Steffensen` (component by component, on the host), `CrossedDelta2`,
  `Crossed2Delta`, `Crossed2Deltabis`, `AlternateDelta2` and
  `Alternate2Delta`, option `Trigger` with the defaults of MTest;
- AccelerationAlgorithm::execute takes a scale of the unknowns, estimated
  by the fixed point solver from its first correction, as the criterion on
  the unknowns of MTest.

FixedPointSolverTest: all the accelerations, except Steffensen's method,
which diverges on this coupled problem, give the solution of the Newton
solver.
